      "lineNbr": 154,
      "author": {
        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-04T07:53:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will fail, see the check at the beginning of util.resolve_build_dir.\n\nWe first test for `build_dir / \u0027project\u0027 / \u0027zmake.yaml\u0027`. If we find it, then build_dir was pointing to an already configured build. If that fails, we try `project_dir / \u0027zmake.yaml\u0027` to see if the user passed a project name. If this passes (note the user doesn\u0027t have to configure the project yet for this to pass) we return the default build directory platform/ec/build/zephyr/...\n\nThen, the actual build function will fail because the directory wouldn\u0027t exist. This would keep the same behavior as current if you were to run:\n$ zmake build /some/garbage/dir",
      "parentUuid": "444ce597_1670c85e",
